/**
 * Pennsylvania Real Estate Practice (45 hours / 3 credits) — module question bank.
 *
 * THE SECOND OF THE TWO COURSES 49 Pa. Code § 35.272(b)(2) NAMES BY TITLE. Together with Real Estate
 * Fundamentals (30 hours / 2 credits) it totals 5 credits / 75 hours, which EXCEEDS the regulatory
 * minimum of "four credits, or 60 hours of instruction" in § 35.272(a)(2). The 30/45 split is a
 * StateCourse decision requiring Commission confirmation — the rule names both courses and assigns hours
 * to neither. See pennsylvania/regulatory/primary-text-readings.md.
 *
 * THIS COURSE IS THE PENNSYLVANIA-SPECIFIC ONE, and § 35.292 is its spine. Every relationship section
 * — §§ 35.312 to 35.316 — opens with "In addition to the duties required in § 35.292." The twelve duties
 * in § 35.292(a) are owed TO ALL CONSUMERS and MAY NOT BE WAIVED; the relationship duties are additions.
 * No item in this bank may present a relationship as subtracting anything from § 35.292.
 *
 * FIVE PERMITTED RELATIONSHIPS, AND ONE OF THEM IS NOT AN AGENCY. Seller's agent, buyer's agent, dual
 * agent, designated agent, and TRANSACTION LICENSEE — who under § 35.316 "is not acting as an agent or
 * advocate for the consumer" and owes only LIMITED confidentiality: three listed items, and nothing else.
 * Several items exist specifically to catch a student who assumes limited confidentiality is a general
 * duty.
 *
 * THE MATERIAL DEFECT EXCEPTION IS WRITTEN INSIDE THE CONFIDENTIALITY DUTY. § 35.312(a)(2), for a
 * seller's agent: "Confidentiality, except that a licensee has a duty to reveal known material defects
 * about the property." § 35.314(b)(3) states the same for a dual agent. There is no conflict to resolve
 * — confidentiality never covered it.
 *
 * ITEM SECURITY AND GRADING. § 35.358(b)(2): "A prelicensure course must be graded by proctored
 * examination." These items are NOT that examination — they gate progression and are visible by design.
 * The 80 percent engagement threshold is a StateCourse standard; Chapter 35 prescribes no in-module score.
 *
 * Each module carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation items. The correct
 * answer is authored at index 0 and permuted deterministically per item id at delivery. The public
 * delivery path strips correctChoice and rationale, and a test proves it.
 *
 * WHAT WAS NOT OBTAINED, AND WHICH THEREFORE APPEARS IN NO ITEM: the Real Estate Licensing and
 * Registration Act (63 P.S. §§ 455.101—455.902); 68 Pa.C.S. Chapter 73 (Real Estate Seller Disclosure
 * Law); the Commission's content outlines for either named course; THE VERBATIM TEXT OF THE §§ 35.336—
 * 35.339 CONSUMER DISCLOSURE SUMMARIES; THE ITEMISED DISCLOSURES IN § 35.335a; the Pennsylvania Landlord
 * and Tenant Act; Pennsylvania's realty transfer tax statutes; ARELLO's distance education standards;
 * USPAP; and TILA, RESPA, TRID, ECOA and the federal Fair Housing Act. No item asks a student to recall
 * or reproduce anything from any of them.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — NOT APPROVED. No Pennsylvania prelicensing credit is available.
 */

